{
  "generated_description": "The Accidental Deaths & Suicides in India (ADSI) - 2024 catalog compiles police-recorded information on natural and unnatural accidents, traffic accidents, and suicides. It covers major causes and means, including traffic accidents, drowning, lightning, heart attacks, accidental fire, falls, and poisoning, alongside suicide causes such as family problems, illness, and bankruptcy or indebtedness. The catalog presents age and gender-wise distributions for all-India coverage, supporting analysis of trends and prevention planning by the Ministry of Home Affairs and the National Crime Records Bureau (NCRB).",
  "generated_sector": "Home Affairs and Enforcement; Enforcement Organizations"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles the answers to Rajya Sabha questions for Session 270, sourced from various ministries and departments. It supports research and monitoring of parliamentary responses across policy areas, enabling users to track government positions, actions, and information provided in the House. Published under the Rajya Sabha, the coverage pertains to questions and answers for Session 270, with content drawn from across India.",
  "generated_sector": "Parliament Of india; Rajya Sabha"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers assistance and support for Scouting and Guiding organizations in India, focusing on youth development through structured, value-based programmes. It supports activities that strengthen youth leadership and participation, with an emphasis on competent leadership, effective communication, and the use of technology and efficient management. The initiatives are published by the Ministry of Youth Affairs and Sports; Department of Youth Affairs and are intended to help Scouting and Guiding organizations expand and sustain their youth movement across India.",
  "generated_sector": "Youth and Sports; Youth Affairs"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Year-wise budget allocations for the Department of Sports are compiled for the period 2012-13 to 2021-22, covering funding for its schemes. The catalog supports analysis of trends in sports financing and helps in monitoring allocation patterns across years. It is published by the Ministry of Youth Affairs and Sports, Department of Sports, and is focused on India-wide scheme budgets.",
  "generated_sector": "Youth and Sports; Games"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Budgets for the schemes of the Department of Youth Affairs under the Ministry of Youth Affairs and Sports are compiled for use in planning, monitoring and public accountability. The catalog focuses on budgetary allocations and related scheme-level financial information for youth development initiatives. It covers India-wide implementation, supporting stakeholders such as policymakers, researchers and civil society in tracking funding priorities for youth programmes.",
  "generated_sector": "Finance; Revenue"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Weekly COVID 19 testing data for India focuses on positivity rate, highlighting districts with more than 10% positivity. Published by the Ministry of Health and Family Welfare, Department of Health Research, and the Indian Council of Medical Research (ICMR), it supports timely monitoring of testing outcomes and identification of areas with higher transmission indicators. The catalog is useful for public health surveillance, risk assessment, and guiding targeted interventions based on district-level trends over time.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Crime in India (CII) - 2024 compiles police and crime statistics for India, covering cognizable crimes registered, BNS/IPC crimes, and cases under Special and Local Laws. It tracks key categories such as violent crimes, murder and culpable homicide not amounting to murder, kidnapping and abduction, and related victim and incident details, along with charge-sheet and disposal of cases. Published by the Ministry of Home Affairs and the National Crime Records Bureau (NCRB), it supports analysis of crime trends and reporting across major crime types and affected groups.",
  "generated_sector": "Home Affairs and Enforcement; Police"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Annotated image data for crop diseases and pests across India supports research and development in plant protection. The collection is designed for computer vision and related analytics to identify and classify pests and disease symptoms from images. It can be used to train and evaluate machine learning models, assist agronomy and extension workflows, and strengthen decision support for crop health monitoring. Published under the Ministry of Agriculture and Farmers Welfare, Department of Agricultural Research and Education (DARE), and the Indian Council of Agricultural Research (ICAR).",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Plant Protection"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together district-level information on the number of fertilizer dealers, covering both retailers and wholesalers across India. It supports analysis of fertilizer distribution networks and market availability, helping stakeholders understand dealer density by district for planning, monitoring, and policy interventions. Published under the Ministry of Chemicals and Fertilizers, Department of Fertilizers, the resources are useful for supply-side assessments and strengthening last-mile access to fertilizer inputs.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Fertilizers"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Year-wise subsidy details for fertilizer products in India, covering key inputs such as UREA (indigenous and imported) and P and K (indigenous and imported). The catalog supports analysis of fertilizer subsidy trends over time and helps stakeholders assess policy support, import versus domestic components, and changes in subsidy allocation. Published by the Ministry of Chemicals and Fertilizers, Department of Fertilizers, it is useful for researchers, analysts, and policymakers tracking fertilizer pricing and subsidy impacts.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Fertilizers"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides details of Antiretroviral Treatment (ART) centres across India, supporting identification of HIV/AIDS care facilities. It covers facility-level information such as ART centre name, address, and contact details, along with location attributes like State and District. These records help program managers, health workers, and researchers locate treatment points and plan service delivery under the National AIDS Control Organisation (NACO) and the Department of AIDS Control. The focus is on facility granularity for India.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog focuses on epidemic diseases reported under the Nashik Municipal Corporation, supporting public health monitoring and local disease surveillance. It brings together annual records that help track occurrence and trends of epidemic conditions for municipal planning and response. The information is relevant for health administrators, researchers, and policy makers working on prevention, preparedness, and community-level interventions in Nashik. The scope covers Nashik, Maharashtra, and is organized on an annual basis.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles expenditure data for the schemes of the Department of Youth Affairs under the Ministry of Youth Affairs and Sports. It supports monitoring and analysis of public spending on youth-focused initiatives, helping stakeholders assess allocation patterns and scheme-wise financial outlays. The coverage is for India, reflecting government expenditure across the country.",
  "generated_sector": "Finance; Revenue"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides product-wise and group-wise export data for major chemicals from India, covering both quantity and value. It spans key chemical categories such as Alkali Chemicals, Dyes & Dyestuff, Inorganic Chemicals, Organic Chemicals, and Pesticides & Insecticides. Published by the Ministry of Chemicals and Fertilizers, Department of Chemicals and Petrochemicals, the collection supports trade analysis, market monitoring, and policy and industry planning for chemical exports.",
  "generated_sector": "Industries; Chemicals and Petrochemicals"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers product-wise and group-wise exports of major petrochemicals from India, reporting both quantity and value. It organizes petrochemical items into groups such as Aromatics, Olefins, Polymers, Performance Plastics, Synthetic Fibres, Synthetic Rubber (ELASTOMERS), and Synthetic Detergent Intermediates, enabling analysis across chemical categories. Published by the Ministry of Chemicals and Fertilizers, Department of Chemicals and Petrochemicals, the collection supports trade monitoring, market research, and policy and industry planning for petrochemical exports.",
  "generated_sector": "Industries; Chemicals and Petrochemicals"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides a list of Gram Panchayats along with their LGD codes for Ahilyanagar, supporting accurate identification and linkage of local governance units in administrative and planning workflows. It is useful for applications that require standardized Panchayati Raj unit codes, such as data integration, reporting, and mapping of rural local bodies. The focus is on rural governance at the Gram Panchayat level under the Panchayati Raj framework.",
  "generated_sector": "Rural; Panchayati Raj"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together health-related data for Nashik, covering information managed by the Nashik Municipal Corporation. It focuses on health service utilization and patient-related indicators, supporting monitoring of local health needs and planning of municipal health interventions. The datasets align with Annual Health Survey (AHS) themes and can be used by public health analysts, researchers, and administrators to track trends and assess service delivery at the city level in Maharashtra.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers country-wise information on the import of fertilizers into India, focusing on major fertilizer types such as Urea, DAP, MAP, MOP, NP and NPK. It supports analysis of fertilizer supply patterns and demand-side dependencies for agricultural inputs. The data is published by the Ministry of Chemicals and Fertilizers, Department of Fertilizers, and is useful for policymakers, researchers and industry stakeholders tracking chemical fertilizer trade and composition.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Fertilizers"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers product-wise and group-wise imports of major chemicals into India, reported in both quantity and value. It brings together imports across major chemical groupings such as Alkali Chemicals, Dyes & Dyestuff, Inorganic Chemicals, Organic Chemicals, and Pesticides & Insecticides, enabling analysis of trade patterns by product and chemical category. Published by the Ministry of Chemicals and Fertilizers, Department of Chemicals and Petrochemicals, it supports market research, policy monitoring, and supply-chain planning for chemical inputs.",
  "generated_sector": "Industries; Chemicals and Petrochemicals"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers product-wise and group-wise imports of major petrochemicals into India, capturing both quantity and value. It spans key petrochemical categories such as Aromatics, Olefins, Polymers, Synthetic Fibres, Synthetic Rubber (ELASTOMERS), Performance Plastics, and detergent and fibre intermediates. The series supports trade analysis, supply-chain planning, and policy monitoring for the petrochemicals sector under the Ministry of Chemicals and Fertilizers, Department of Chemicals and Petrochemicals.",
  "generated_sector": "Industries; Chemicals and Petrochemicals"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers international cooperation activities under the International Youth Exchange Programme, focusing on youth delegation participation. It supports eligible youth with financial assistance for airfare and space rent on a reimbursement basis, enabling cross-border exposure and exchange. Published by the Ministry of Youth Affairs and Sports; Department of Youth Affairs, the resources are intended for planning, participation, and reimbursement-related processes. The geographic coverage is India, supporting youth delegations connected to international exchange.",
  "generated_sector": "Youth and Sports; Youth Affairs"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The Khelo India Scheme catalog brings together information on sports infrastructure projects sanctioned under the Khelo India scheme by the Government of India for promotion of sports. It supports understanding of how sports facilities are planned and enabled across India, useful for monitoring implementation and assessing investment in grassroots and competitive sports. The catalog is published by the Ministry of Youth Affairs and Sports, Department of Sports, and focuses on project-level infrastructure sanctioned under the scheme.",
  "generated_sector": "Sports and Youth Affairs; Youth and Sports"
}

{
  "generated_description": "MESCOM Gruha Jyothi data provides district- and taluk-wise information on electricity subsidy releases under the Gruha Jyothi scheme by the Government of Karnataka. The catalog supports analysis of subsidy distribution across administrative units and can be used for monitoring coverage, planning outreach, and assessing program delivery at the local level. It is focused on Karnataka and covers subsidy release details for the scheme’s implementation within the state.",
  "generated_sector": "Power and Energy; Renewable"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Monthly import data for chemical fertilizers into India, covering major products such as DAP, MAP, MOP, NPK, TSP and UREA. The catalog tracks quantities by country for each month, supporting analysis of sourcing patterns, import dependence and seasonal trends in fertilizer availability. It is published by the Ministry of Chemicals and Fertilizers, Department of Fertilizers, and is useful for policymakers, researchers and industry stakeholders monitoring fertilizer trade flows.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Fertilizers"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Month wise and port wise import data for chemical fertilizers across India, covering key fertilizer types such as DAP, MAP, MOP, NPK, UREA and TSP. The catalog supports analysis of import flows by month and by port, helping track supply trends, seasonal movement, and sourcing patterns for fertilizer inputs. Published by the Ministry of Chemicals and Fertilizers, Department of Fertilizers, it is useful for policy monitoring, market intelligence, and planning for fertilizer availability.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Fertilizers"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides location metadata for the Nashik Police Station, including its address along with latitude and longitude coordinates. It supports use cases such as navigation, geocoding, and locating the police station for public access and service delivery. The information is relevant for India-wide applications that need accurate point locations for policing infrastructure. The focus is on a single police station location rather than multi-station or district-level coverage.",
  "generated_sector": "Home Affairs and Enforcement; Police"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The National Ethics Committee Registry for Bio-medical and Health Research supports the registration of ethics committees that review biomedical and health research involving human participants. It is administered by the Department of Health Research under the Ministry of Health and Family Welfare, in line with the New Drugs and Clinical Trials Rules-2019, which require ethics committees to register with the designated authority. The registry facilitates ethical oversight and compliance for biomedical and health research across India.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The National Programme for Youth and Adolescent Development (NPYAD) supports youth and adolescent development initiatives across India. It is formulated by merging four 100% central sector grants-in-aid schemes under the Ministry of Youth Affairs and Sports during the 10th Plan, bringing together activities related to youth promotion, training, and national integration. The catalog helps track programme focus areas and use cases such as youth capacity building and development interventions for adolescents and young people.",
  "generated_sector": "Youth and Sports; Youth Affairs"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The National Young Leaders Programme (NYLP) supports youth leadership development across India. It is a Central Sector Scheme introduced in December 2014, designed to build leadership qualities and help young participants realize their full potential while contributing to nation-building. The programme is implemented by the Ministry of Youth Affairs and Sports, Department of Youth Affairs, and is intended for youth-focused capacity building and leadership-oriented engagement.",
  "generated_sector": "Youth and Sports; Youth Affairs"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The National Youth Corps catalog brings together information on the Government’s youth volunteer scheme launched during the financial year 2010-11 to channel youth energy towards nation building. It is aligned with the President’s Address to both Houses of Parliament in June 2009 and the Prime Minister’s announcement in October 2009 for Jammu & Kashmir. Managed by the Ministry of Youth Affairs and Sports; Department of Youth Affairs, the initiative supports youth engagement and service activities across India.",
  "generated_sector": "Youth and Sports; Youth Affairs"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Year-wise national estimates of HIV key indicators with uncertainty bounds are compiled for India. The catalog covers core measures such as estimated number of people living with HIV (PLHIV), estimated adult HIV prevalence, annual new HIV infections, annual AIDS-related deaths, and estimated ART need, disaggregated by adults (15+) and children under 15 and by sex where applicable. These indicators support monitoring of the HIV epidemic and program planning by the Ministry of Health and Family Welfare, Department of AIDS Control, and National AIDS Control Organisation (NACO).",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The Nehru Yuva Kendra Sangathan (NYKS) catalog brings together open data related to grassroots youth development initiatives across India. It supports understanding of how rural youth are engaged in nation-building through programs aimed at personality development and skill building. Published under the Ministry of Youth Affairs and Sports (Department of Youth Affairs), the catalog is useful for monitoring participation, planning youth-focused interventions, and informing policy and program evaluation for youth affairs.",
  "generated_sector": "Youth and Sports; Youth Affairs"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers PM Awas Yojana initiatives implemented for Zilla Parishad Ahilyanagar, focusing on rural housing support. It brings together information relevant to planning and monitoring housing under the scheme, supporting delivery of eligible housing benefits. The scope is limited to Ahilyanagar, reflecting the local implementation context of the Zilla Parishad. The catalog is intended for stakeholders seeking scheme-related insights for rural housing delivery at the district level.",
  "generated_sector": "Housing; Rural Housing"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Monthly production statistics for chemical fertilizers in India, presented product-wise and month-wise. The catalog covers key fertilizer types such as CAN, DAP, UREA, and SSP, along with their nutrient composition in terms of N, P and K. It supports analysis of production trends, monitoring of fertilizer supply by product, and planning for agricultural inputs through the year. Published by the Ministry of Chemicals and Fertilizers, Department of Fertilizers.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Fertilizers"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together product-wise and group-wise production statistics for major chemicals in India, compiled from monthly production returns submitted by manufacturers to the Department of Chemicals and Petrochemicals. It supports analysis of trends across chemical categories such as inorganic and organic chemicals, alkali and dyestuff, and related inputs including dyes, pesticides and insecticides. Useful for industry monitoring, policy and planning, and market research by tracking output over time at product and group levels under the Ministry of Chemicals and Fertilizers.",
  "generated_sector": "Industries; Chemicals and Petrochemicals"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together product-wise and group-wise production statistics for major petrochemicals in India, compiled from monthly production returns submitted by manufacturers. It supports analysis of trends across key petrochemical categories such as aromatics, olefins, intermediates, polymers, elastomers, and related synthetic products. Published by the Department of Chemicals and Petrochemicals under the Ministry of Chemicals and Fertilizers, the collection is useful for industry monitoring, policy review, and market and capacity assessments based on aggregated production figures.",
  "generated_sector": "Industries; Chemicals and Petrochemicals"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Tracks the requirement and availability of major fertilizer products such as DAP, MAP, MOP, TSP, NPK and UREA. The catalog supports month-wise and state-wise monitoring of fertilizer demand and supply, useful for planning procurement, distribution and policy interventions in the fertilizer sector. Published by the Ministry of Chemicals and Fertilizers, Department of Fertilizers, it covers fertilizer availability and requirement across India.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Fertilizers"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together scheme-wise expenditure data for the schemes of the Department of Sports under the Ministry of Youth Affairs and Sports. It covers budget allocation, revised estimates, and actual expenditure for sports schemes, enabling year-on-year tracking of financial outlays and spending performance. The information supports monitoring, budgeting analysis, and policy review for sports programme implementation across India.",
  "generated_sector": "Youth and Sports; Games"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together state-wise and month-wise information on the requirement and availability of major chemical fertilizers, including DAP, MAP, MOP, TSP, NPK and UREA. It supports monitoring of fertilizer supply and demand patterns across India and helps stakeholders plan procurement, distribution and inventory management. Published by the Ministry of Chemicals and Fertilizers, Department of Fertilizers, the resources enable analysis at state level with monthly granularity for key fertilizer product categories.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Fertilizers"
}

{
  "generated_description": "State/UT-wise estimates of annual AIDS-related deaths are provided for India, including uncertainty bounds to reflect estimation variability. The catalog supports monitoring of HIV/AIDS mortality trends and risk assessment at subnational level for public health planning and evaluation. It is published by the Ministry of Health and Family Welfare through the Department of AIDS Control and the National AIDS Control Organisation (NACO).",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "State/UT-wise estimates of annual new HIV infections among adults (15+ years) are provided for India, including uncertainty bounds to support interpretation of trends. The indicators focus on HIV/AIDS burden and are useful for monitoring epidemic dynamics, planning prevention and care interventions, and evaluating program impact. Published by the Ministry of Health and Family Welfare through the Department of AIDS Control and the National AIDS Control Organisation (NACO), the data supports subnational public health decision-making across States/UTs.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "State/UT-wise estimates of adult (15-49 years) HIV prevalence (%) are provided for India, along with uncertainty bounds to support interpretation of epidemic levels. The indicator reflects the share of adults living with HIV within the 15-49 years age group, expressed as a percentage. Published by the Ministry of Health and Family Welfare, Department of AIDS Control, and the National AIDS Control Organisation (NACO), these estimates support planning, monitoring, and evaluation of HIV prevention and control efforts across States/UTs.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together State/UT-wise estimates of the need for ART among adults aged 15+ years, including uncertainty bounds. It supports planning and monitoring of HIV treatment delivery by estimating the total number of people who may require ART based on national initiation guidelines. The estimates reflect changes in clinical criteria over time, using CD4 thresholds up to 2008 and revised thresholds during 2009–2011. Published by the Ministry of Health and Family Welfare, Department of AIDS Control, and NACO for use in health program decision-making across India.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "State/UT-wise estimates of HIV infections in India are provided with uncertainty bounds for people living with HIV (PLHIV), covering both adults and children. The series supports assessing disease burden, forecasting treatment needs, and planning testing and prevention programmes across different States/UTs. Published by the Ministry of Health and Family Welfare, Department of AIDS Control, and the National AIDS Control Organisation (NACO), the estimates help target interventions where the HIV burden is highest.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles State/UT-wise HIV prevalence (%) from HIV Sentinel Surveillance across multiple population groups, including general population (ANC attendees) and high-risk groups such as FSW, MSM, TG, and IDU, along with bridge populations like SMM and LDT. It supports monitoring of HIV burden and risk patterns for targeted public health planning and program evaluation. Published by the Ministry of Health and Family Welfare through the Department of AIDS Control and NACO, the data covers HIV prevalence across India.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides State/UT-wise estimates of mothers needing Prevention of Parent to Child Transmission of HIV (PPTCT), along with uncertainty bounds. It supports monitoring of HIV transmission risks to children and planning PPTCT services that protect women, newborns, and families. Published by the Ministry of Health and Family Welfare, Department of AIDS Control, and the National AIDS Control Organisation (NACO), the data covers India and is presented at the State/UT level.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "State/UT-wise estimates of the need for anti-retro-viral treatment (ART) for children under 15 years are provided with uncertainty bounds. The indicators support planning and monitoring of HIV/AIDS care by quantifying the estimated treatment requirement and the associated uncertainty for each State/UT across India. Published by the Ministry of Health and Family Welfare, Department of AIDS Control, and the National AIDS Control Organisation (NACO), the data can be used for resource allocation, program evaluation, and policy decision-making for pediatric ART services.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers the TB program under the Nashik Municipal Corporation, focusing on tuberculosis control activities and related health service delivery. It supports use cases such as monitoring program implementation, assessing service coverage, and informing planning and reporting for TB prevention and care. The scope is limited to Nashik Municipal Corporation, with data presented on an annual basis. The publishing organization is the Nashik Municipal Corporation, aligned with family welfare and public health objectives.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Vahan provides State/UT-wise information on vehicles registered through RTOs, including details linked to vehicle maker and registration. It supports tracking of vehicle registration trends and related administrative needs such as permit and registration monitoring. Published by the Ministry of Road Transport and Highways, the catalog covers vehicle registration data for India, enabling analysis at the State/UT level for planning, compliance, and policy review.",
  "generated_sector": "Transport; Road Transport"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The Youth Hostel Scheme supports the planning and development of youth hostels across India through a joint effort of the Central and State Governments. It focuses on providing suitable land and enabling construction of hostels to improve access to affordable accommodation and youth-oriented travel and activities. The scheme is administered by the Ministry of Youth Affairs and Sports, Department of Youth Affairs, and is relevant for stakeholders involved in youth services, infrastructure planning, and hostel operations.",
  "generated_sector": "Youth and Sports; Youth Affairs"
}
